Most 1-minute moves are under 2 bps. Large moves need strong evidence from velocity, tape imbalance, funding proximity, or cross-asset leadership. Near funding (under 90 minutes) can produce mean reversion. High velocity or shock suggests continuation but often exhausts quickly. Tape imbalance shows immediate pressure but may be noise. Be skeptical of direction calls without multiple confirming signals.
